@page "/privacy"

<PageTitle>Privacy notice</PageTitle>

<h1>Privacy notice</h1>

<p class="lead">How CohortCompanion treats students who join a live session.</p>

<h2 class="h4">What we collect</h2>
<ul>
    <li>The nickname you type.</li>
    <li>The answers you give during the session.</li>
    <li>A random code stored on your device, so you can reconnect if your phone sleeps or you refresh the page.</li>
</ul>
<p>Use a nickname. Please don't enter your full name or student ID.</p>

<h2 class="h4">How long we keep it</h2>
<p>
    Only while the session is running. When the instructor ends the session, your nickname and answers are deleted.
    If a session is abandoned, they're deleted automatically after an hour without activity. What stays is totals for
    each question, such as how many people chose each option, with no nicknames attached.
</p>

<h2 class="h4">What it's used for</h2>
<p>
    Only for running the session in class. Nothing you do here is used for grading or advertising, and there are no
    analytics, advertising, or third-party scripts on student pages.
</p>

<h2 class="h4">Who can see your answers</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Your instructor can see your nickname and your answers while the session is running.</li>
    <li>Word clouds and fill-in-the-blank results are shown to the class as totals, without nicknames.</li>
    <li>If a quiz has a leaderboard, the top five nicknames and scores appear on the projector. Your own rank appears only on your device.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="h4">Cookies</h2>
<p>Students get no cookies. The only thing stored on your device is the reconnect code, and it stops working when the session ends.</p>

<h2 class="h4">Questions</h2>
<p>Ask your instructor, who can pass questions on to the people running this service.</p>
